{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789956990,"nonce":"5Mv7yZAkO0IAt2W3nD1hTof0mmE=","title":"Python: `for x in s` over a set-typed value iterates the raw storage list","message":"Reproducer (zypy run, LLVM on or off):\n\n    def run2():\n        s = set([3, 1, 2])\n        total = 0\n        for x in s:\n            total += x\n        return total\n    print(run2())\n\nCPython prints 6; zypy raises `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s):\n'int' and 'NoneType'`. With `s` a `frozenset` parameter (`run(s: Set)`)\nit raises `TypeError: 'object' object is not subscriptable` instead.\n\nCause: `Lowerer::for_items` has no `Ty::Set` arm. The set falls through\nto the generic sequence path: `len` is the storage list's length (the\nhash index at slot 0 counts), and `index_value` on `Ty::Set` reaches\nthe `_ =\u003e zb_any_getitem_i64` arm with the raw list header as the\nobject. `for_items` snapshots `Ty::Object | Ty::Dict(_)` but not sets,\nand `iterable()` coerces a set with `zb_set_items`, which the for loop\nnever calls.\n\nNo conformance case iterates a set with a for statement (set/basics.py\nand set/frozenset.py only sort or comprehend). meteor-contest's\n`for ci in fp` (fp: frozenset) only works because `fp` is typed Object.\n\nFix belongs with the typed iteration work (a253f9f cluster): iterate\nthe storage list from slot 1 to its length in place, no snapshot, since\nPython forbids mutating a set while iterating it.","files":null}]}